**Packet saved to `docs/content-analysis/entity-gaps/Zach-Bryan.md` — verdict: PASS on the entity-gap rubric (43/100), but a clear green light for the queued draft as a personality-analysis play.** Tonight's pipeline run (stage 0.5 was waiting on this) now has its brief.

The short version: Zach Bryan is not a biography-of-record opportunity — he has a personal Wikipedia page, dedicated bios at Biography.com, Billboard, AllMusic, and IMDb, and celebrity press maintains dating-history explainers that update within days. That's a −20 penalty and a 4/25 on SERP weakness. But he scored the highest of any mega-famous pass in the folder (Khabib 29, Jordan 32, Mercury 33) because everything else is unusually strong:

- **Catalysts are live right now**: *With Heaven on Top* hit #1 in January (reported as his final major-label album), the "With Heaven On Tour" stadium run goes through October 10 (AT&T Stadium was 8 days ago), and he married Samantha Leonard on NYE in Spain.
- **The personality-type SERP is nearly empty** — the incumbents are Personality Database crowd votes and a Boo.world page that's actually Zachery Ty Bryan, the Home Improvement actor. Nobody owns an editorial personality analysis.
- **Source depth is elite**: two Rolling Stone covers (including the Springsteen Musicians-on-Musicians conversation), plus a huge self-authored record since he skips interviews and narrates his life on X.

The organizing contradiction I handed the pipeline: **the most anti-machine man in American music built the biggest machine in it** — fought Ticketmaster, quit TikTok, is leaving his label, while setting the all-time U.S. attendance record (112,408 at Michigan Stadium). Radical self-disclosure on his own terms, combustible when control slips (the 2023 arrest, "Skin," the DHS fight over "Bad News").

The packet also fences off the landmines: marriage-trouble speculation (gossip-press inference only), the LaPaglia allegations (attribute everything, assert nothing), his stale official bio (wrong age and service length), and the actor name-collision in sourcing.

